   "titulo": "Future I",
   "texto": [
    "It is formed with **werden** conjugated and infinitive at the end: **In zwei Jahren werde ich mein Studium abschließen** (within two years I will complete my studies). It is used for plans, promises and predictions. In the day to day the present is used more with a word of time: **Nächstes Jahr fahre ich nach Italien** (next year I go to Italy)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Wohl supposition",
   "texto": [
    "To say something likely, **werden** + **wohl** + infinitive: **Er wird wohl krank sein** is used (probably ill). «Probably.» is used with the idea of **wohl** or **vermutlich**.",
    "Eye with the false friend: **wohl** does not mean «Good.»; it means «Probably.»."
   ]
